Now, moving on to the $10 bills. He has 10 of them. Each $10 bill is 10 dollars, so 10 times 10... that should be 100 dollars. So, the $10 bills contribute 100 dollars.

Now, to find the total amount of money Meghan has, I need to add up the amounts from each type of bill. So, that would be the $100 bills (200) plus the $50 bills (250) plus the $10 bills (100). Let me write that out:

